# File: tests/features/add_greeting_vowel_count_library_helper.feature
# Generated from: specs/203-add-greeting-vowel-count-library-helper/requirements.md
Feature: Count ASCII vowels in the completed greeting

  @SCN001
  Scenario: Count ASCII vowels in the completed greeting
    Given the installed nmg_sdlc_smoke package
    When greeting_vowel_count is called with Ada and with AEIOU aeiou
    Then the results are the Python int values 4 and 12

  @SCN002
  Scenario: Ignore characters outside the ten ASCII vowels
    Given the installed nmg_sdlc_smoke package
    When greeting_vowel_count is called with Bcd, Ady, Émile spelled with precomposed U+00C9, and fullwidth U+FF21 U+FF44 U+FF41
    Then the results are 2, 3, 4, and 2

  @SCN003
  Scenario: Preserve invalid-name behavior
    Given the invalid names empty, space-tab, None, and 42
    When greeting_vowel_count is called with each invalid name
    Then each call raises ValueError with message name must not be blank

  @SCN004
  Scenario: Expose and document the helper
    Given the README Library section
    When the README Library example runs and prints greeting_vowel_count of Ada
    Then it prints 4 and greeting_vowel_count is listed in nmg_sdlc_smoke.__all__
    And the README documents the ASCII vowel set, completed-greeting scope, and inherited invalid-name error
